cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this model in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "AnimDens NetLogo"
abstract: "An agent-based model of surveyors counting animals with belt-transect, stationary-point-count and roving (random path) techniques. It demonstrates how non-instantaneous sampling overestimates counts when animals move relative to the surveyor, and provides a calculator that corrects field counts for that bias. NetLogo implementation of the AnimDens model of Ward-Paige et al. (2010), originally written in R."
authors:
  - family-names: "Pais"
    given-names: "Miguel Pessanha"
    # TODO: ORCID not recorded anywhere in this repository — fill it in rather
    # than leaving it out; a citation widget without one cannot disambiguate.
    affiliation: "Faculdade de Ciências, Universidade de Lisboa"
  - family-names: "Ward-Paige"
    given-names: "Christine A."
    # TODO: ORCID and affiliation for the second author are not recorded in
